TITLE:: PianoRollNote
SUMMARY:: One recorded note in the piano roll with selection, part assignment, and grid editing.
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events
RELATED:: Classes/PianoRoll, Classes/PlayableNote, Classes/Event

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::PianoRollNote:: wraps a LINK::Classes/PlayableNote:: and a LINK::Classes/Event:: with piano-roll UI callbacks (view creation, selection highlighting, part colours, and view repositioning after timing edits). Commands such as LINK::Classes/AmpCommand:: write keys onto the composed LINK::Classes/Event:: (for example CODE::\amp::) and keep the LINK::Classes/PlayableNote:: in sync. LINK::Classes/PianoRoll:: creates instances when recording MIDI or dev-mode fake notes.

NOTE::
You can run the unit tests for TELETYPE::PianoRollNote:: by running:
CODE::
(
UnitTest.reportPasses_(false);
PianoRollNoteUnitTests.run;
)
::
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a TELETYPE::PianoRollNote::.

ARGUMENT:: startTime
Note-on time in beats.

ARGUMENT:: noteNumber
MIDI note number.

ARGUMENT:: velocity
MIDI velocity.

ARGUMENT:: viewFunc
LINK::Classes/Function:: called from LINK::#-stop:: to create the note's LINK::Classes/View::.

ARGUMENT:: selectFunc
LINK::Classes/Function:: called when the note becomes selected.

ARGUMENT:: deselectFunc
LINK::Classes/Function:: called when the note is deselected.

ARGUMENT:: setPart1Func
LINK::Classes/Function:: called when part 1 is assigned to a selected note.

ARGUMENT:: setPart2Func
LINK::Classes/Function:: called when part 2 is assigned to a selected note.

ARGUMENT:: setPart3Func
LINK::Classes/Function:: called when part 3 is assigned to a selected note.

ARGUMENT:: setPart4Func
LINK::Classes/Function:: called when part 4 is assigned to a selected note.

ARGUMENT:: moveFunc
LINK::Classes/Function:: called after timing edits with CODE::func.value(view, startTime, stopTime)::.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: amp_
Clips CODE::value:: to CODE::0::–CODE::1::, stores it as CODE::\amp:: on the composed LINK::Classes/Event::, and sets MIDI velocity to CODE::value.linlin(0, 1, 0, 127):: rounded to an LINK::Classes/Integer::.

ARGUMENT:: value
A LINK::Classes/SimpleNumber:: amplitude. Values outside CODE::0:: to CODE::1:: are clipped silently.

METHOD:: deselect
Clears selection and invokes the deselect callback.

METHOD:: event
The composed LINK::Classes/Event::, created with no parent so default pattern keys such as CODE::\amp:: are unset until a command writes them.

RETURNS::
An LINK::Classes/Event::.

METHOD:: isSelected
Returns whether this note is currently selected.

METHOD:: noteNumber
Returns the wrapped note's MIDI note number.

METHOD:: nudgeLeft
Moves the note one grid step left at CODE::resolution:: beats. If the start time is already on the grid, subtracts one step; if off-grid, moves to the adjacent grid line to the left. Preserves duration; start time is clamped at beat zero.

ARGUMENT:: resolution
Grid spacing in beats (for example CODE::0.125:: for sixteenth notes in a quarter-note grid).

METHOD:: nudgeRight
Moves the note one grid step right at CODE::resolution:: beats. If the start time is already on the grid, adds one step; if off-grid, moves to the adjacent grid line to the right. Preserves duration; start time is clamped at beat zero.

ARGUMENT:: resolution
Grid spacing in beats.

METHOD:: playableNote
Returns the wrapped LINK::Classes/PlayableNote::.

METHOD:: selectIfEnclosed
Selects or deselects based on whether this note's view lies inside CODE::possiblyEnclosingView::.

ARGUMENT:: possiblyEnclosingView
A LINK::Classes/View:: whose bounds define the selection rectangle.

ARGUMENT:: addToExistingSelection
When true, notes outside the rectangle are left unchanged; when false, they are deselected.

METHOD:: setPartIfSelected
If selected, assigns part CODE::partNumber:: (1–4) and runs the matching part callback.

ARGUMENT:: partNumber
Part index from 1 to 4.

METHOD:: snapToGrid
Snaps the start time to the nearest grid line at CODE::resolution:: beats and shifts the stop time by the same delta so duration is preserved. Start time is clamped at beat zero.

ARGUMENT:: resolution
Grid spacing in beats.

METHOD:: startTime
Returns the note-on time in beats.

METHOD:: stop
Sets the note-off time and schedules creation of the note view.

ARGUMENT:: stopTime
Note-off time in beats.

METHOD:: stopTime
Returns the note-off time in beats.

METHOD:: toggleSelect
Toggles selection and runs the select or deselect callback.

METHOD:: velocity
Returns the wrapped note's velocity.

PRIVATE:: init, prApplyTimeDelta, prIsOnGrid
